  "interpretation": {
    "primary_observation": "Increasing teacher-relax force multiplier from 2.0 to 2.5 while keeping ENERGY_WEIGHT=2.0 improves benchmark-side energy RMSE/E max and F max relative to Stage140 ew2, while preserving ~1.02M atoms/s throughput.",
    "negative_observation": "The same fm2.5/ew2 row slightly worsens F RMSE, C/N rattle RMSD, rattle fmax, and physical score relative to Stage140 ew2; all Stage141 rows still fail physical_gate because rattle relaxed fmax remains ~9 eV/A.",
    "route_decision": "Stage141 shows the loss/deployment measure can move the benchmark Pareto point, but it does not close physical relaxation. Treat fm2.5/ew2 as the benchmark incumbent and Stage140 ew2 as the physical-rattle incumbent. Stage142 should add teacher-relax trajectory volume / curvature-tail coverage before spending architecture complexity, and only then test a minimal representation/projection capacity increment if the fmax tail persists.",
    "document_alignment": "This keeps TECE_design_space Sobolev-measure separation and rTECE_review physical-validation requirements; it remains a fixed-architecture distillation closure test rather than a heuristic architecture change."
